Project: Automated Project Bootstrapping & Process Management
The Power of Infrastructure as Code (IaC)

 - This is a shell script that automates the setup of a student attendance tracker by creating a directory , generating files, configuring and validating.

- The shell script runs on a Linux operating system, the tools used were git and bash, the required file is setup_project.sh

- Clone into the repository, navigate into the repository, make the script executable, then run the script. The script will let you fill in your project name and if you want to update the attendance thresholds.

-After the running the script, a directory named attendance_tracker_{input} is created containing attendance_checker.py, a Helpers/ folder with two files config.json and assets.csv, and a reports/ folder with only 1 file reports.log. 

-If the thresholds are updated , the config.json file will reflect the new warning and failure values enterd by the user.

-To trigger the archive feature, press Ctrl+C while the script is running. The script will catch the interrupted signal, pack the incomplete project directory into an archive named attendance_tracker_{input}_archive, delete the incomplete directory and exit. The archive will be saved in the same folder as setup_project.sh that runs from.

- The script checks if python3 is intalled using python3 --version. If found, it displays a successful message with the installed version. If not found, a warning message is displayed.

-If the project directory already exists, an error message is printed and exits immediately. If invalid threshold value is entered, the script prints an error message and exits already.
